<div class="pdp-badges-sectext">
{{block.settings.badges-html}}	
{%- comment -%} The default product template carries a copy of the product-awards strip inline in badges-html. Only skip the snippet when that inline copy will actually render (product has awards); otherwise render the snippet so the brand-level fallback can show. When the new PDP body (custom.pdp_body_test) is in use, the awards strip is rendered inside the description instead, so skip it here and hide any inline copy. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rf_awards_check = product.metafields.custom.awards.value -%}
{%- assign rf_body_in_use = product.metafields.custom.pdp_body_test.value -%}
{%- if rf_body_in_use != blank -%}
<style>.pdp-badges-sectext .rf-pdp-awards{display:none !important;}</style>
{%- elsif block.settings.badges-html contains 'rf-pdp-awards' and rf_awards_check != blank -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- render 'rf-awards-strip', product: product -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} Restock / low-stock widget (renders only when custom.restock_date is set) {%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'rf-restock-widget', product: product -%}
</div>
{%- comment -%} Awards strip alignment: the theme indents .pdp-badges-sectext by 14px (for the tick list); pull the strip back flush with the assurance tiles / ATC, and tighten the top gap when the strip is the only content. {%- endcomment -%}
<style>
.pdp-badges-sectext .rf-pdp-awards{margin-left:-14px;width:calc(100% + 14px);}
.pdp-badges-sectext:has(> .rf-pdp-awards):not(:has(ul)){margin-top:12px;}
</style>